althy state. So the issue isn\'t with the pod\'s health but possibly with the service\'s configuration or how it\'s handling requests. Checking the dependency graph would help identify if there are any broken links or misconfigured services that the user-service is interacting with. \n\nSo, using get_dependency_graph with a reasonable time frame (like 5 minutes) would provide a visual of the service interactions. If there\'s a service that\'s not properly connected or if there are unexpected dependencies, that could be the root cause. Once the dependency graph is analyzed, if there\'s a problem, the next step would be to check the specific service\'s metrics or logs. But since the user can\'t get logs directly, maybe checking the metrics for the user-service or its dependencies could show any anomalies like high latency or errors.\n</think>\n\nget_dependency_graph  \n"5"  \nThe traces for the user-service show warnings about invalid parent span IDs, which may indicate issues with service dependencies or tracing configuration. By examining the dependency graph, I can identify if there are missing, misconfigured, or unstable connections between the user-service and other microservices. This will help determine if the root cause lies in faulty dependencies or improper tracing setup.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=576, prompt_tokens=3442, total_tokens=4018, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc2b-2348-7742-afc0-02c5316305f6-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3442, 'output_tokens': 576, 'total_tokens': 4018}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0b2deb2d-2ad7-4595-8afa-c