Since the pod is in CrashLoopBackOff, the container is failing to start. I should check the logs to see why. The user tried to get logs earlier but got an error because they didn't specify the pod name. The current pod name is user-service-94d6f89b9-c99rw. So, I need to use kubectl logs with the specific pod name to see the error messages. That will help identify the root cause, like a configuration error, missing dependencies, or a crash in the application code.
