one, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc2c-282b-7270-bbb8-93aa75b640ce-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5020, 'output_tokens': 313, 'total_tokens': 5333}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='79af216c-c104-4e8b-83c1-d239fca8e23d'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user-service pod is in CrashLoopBackOff, which means it\'s crashing repeatedly. The logs I saw earlier didn\'t show any obvious errors, just some warnings about MongoDB and machine IDs. But the pod isn\'t staying up. So, I need to dig deeper.\n\nThe next step is to use kubectl describe pod to get detailed information about the pod. This command will show me the pod\'s status, events, and container details. The events section is especially important because it often lists the reasons why a pod is failing. \n\nLooking at the previous logs, there was a warning about falling back to malloc for counters, which might be related to MongoDB. Maybe the MongoDB connection is problematic. But the describe pod command might show if there are any errors related to the container\'s startup, like failed health checks, missing dependencies, or resource limits. \n\nAlso, the pod\'s status might indicate if the container is crashing due to a specific error, such as an application crash or a missing configuration file. The events could mention things like "CrashLoopBackOff" with more details, or maybe a "Failed" status with a reason. \n\nBy checking the describe output, I can see if there are any recent events that explain the crashes. For example, if the container is failing to start because of an image pull error, or if there\'s a liveness probe failure. This information will help pinpoint the exact cause, whether it\'s a configuration issue, resource problem, or a bug in the application.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod user-service-94d6f89b9-c99rw -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ab38d11e1f6763ee', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 360, 'prompt_tokens': 6016, 'total_tokens': 6376, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc2c-371c-71d0-ab33-f78e562c506c-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod user-service-94d6f89b9-c99rw -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ab38d11e1f6763ee', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6016, 'output_tokens': 360, 'total_tokens': 6376}), ToolMessage(content='Name:             user-service-94d6f89b9-c99rw\nNamespace:        social-network\nPriority:         0\nService Account:  default\nNode:             node0.htliang2-agent.insai-pg0.apt.emulab.net/128.110.96.31\nStart Time:       Tue, 17 Mar 2026 14:18:50 +0000\nLabels:           app=user-service\n                  pod-template-hash=94d6f89b9\n                  service=user-service\nAnnotations:      <none>\nStatus:           Running\nIP:               10.244.0.71\nIPs:\n  IP:           10.244.0.71\nControlled By:  ReplicaSet/user-service-94d6f89b9\nContainers:\n  user-service:\n    Container ID:  docker://4381254fc9636b61c546038b3fd7e349f4065843fa3b5c6c204ed3b54323fca4\n    Image:         docker.io/deathstarbench/social-network-microservices:latest\n    Image ID:      docker-pullable://deathstarbench/social-network-microservices@sha256:a845266e98ce15d204ee7b98d41a2a95820af525013ce70f14104f5b9b5e92b6\n    Port:          9090/TCP\n    Host Port:     0/TCP\n    Command:\n      UserService\n    State:          Running\n      Started:      