ange and memory limits. This ensures that all references in the container\'s volumeMounts are correctly matched with the volumes in the template\'s spec. That way, the Deployment will be valid and the pod should start correctly without the previous errors.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \nreasoning: The error indicates missing volume definitions for `user-service-config`. The original Deployment includes this volume as a ConfigMap. To fix the patch, I must include the full volume definition in the template\'s spec, along with the container\'s volume mounts.  \n\ntool_call:  \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: user-service\\n  namespace: social-network\\nspec:\\n  selector:\\n    matchLabels:\\n      service: user-service\\n  template:\\n    metadata:\\n      labels:\\n        service: user-service\\n        app: user-service\\n    spec:\\n      containers:\\n      - name: user-service\\n        image: docker.io/deathstarbench/social-network-microservices:latest\\n        command:\\n        - UserService\\n        ports:\\n        - containerPort: 9090\\n          protocol: TCP\\n        livenessProbe:\\n          httpGet:\\n            port: 9090\\n            path: /healthz\\n        resources:\\n          limits:\\n            memory: 512Mi\\n        volumeMounts:\\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/jaeger-config.yml\\n          name: user-service-config\\n          subPath: jaeger-config.yml\\n        - mountPath: /social-network-microservices/config/service-config.json\\n          name: user-service-config\\n          subPath: service-config.json\\n      volumes:\\n      - configMap:\\n          defaultMode: 420\\n          name: user-service\\n        name: user-service-config\\nEOF"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'