 these labels, so the Deployment couldn\'t be validated. Therefore, the next step is to generate a correct patch that includes both the livenessProbe, resources, and the required labels, ensuring the selector matches the updated labels.\n\nI should use the exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool again but this time provide a complete patch that includes all necessary changes. This will ensure that the Deployment is valid and the changes are applied correctly without further errors.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely  \nreasoning: The previous patch failed because it didn\'t preserve the required selector/label synchronization in the Deployment. I need to apply a complete patch that:  \n1. Updates the liveness probe port to `9090`.  \n2. Adds memory limits (`512Mi`).  \n3. Preserves the existing selector/label matching between `spec.selector` and `spec.template.metadata.labels`.  \n\ntool_call:  \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl apply -f - <<EOF\\napiVersion: apps/v1\\nkind: Deployment\\nmetadata:\\n  name: user-service\\n  namespace: social-network\\nspec:\\n  selector:\\n    matchLabels:\\n      service: user-service\\n  template:\\n    metadata:\\n      labels:\\n        service: user-service\\n        app: user-service\\n    spec:\\n      containers:\\n      - name: user-service\\n        livenessProbe:\\n          httpGet:\\n            port: 9090\\n        resources:\\n          limits:\\n            memory: 512Mi\\nEOF"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 578, 'prompt_tokens': 7468, 'total_tokens': 8046, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc2d-856b-7ef3-86a4-26260c7aba4d-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_toke